# Commit and push after changes

When you finish implementation work in this repository, **always commit and push** without waiting for the user to ask.

## When to commit and push

Do this at the end of a task when you changed tracked files (code, skin XML, addon versions, changelog, docs the user requested, etc.).

Skip only when:
- There are no file changes to commit
- The user explicitly said not to commit or push in that message
- The task was read-only (questions, review, no edits)

## Workflow

1. Run `git status`, `git diff`, and `git log -1` to see scope and message style
2. Stage relevant files only — never `__pycache__/`, `*.pyc`, `dist/`, secrets, or other ignored artifacts
3. Write a concise commit message focused on **why**
4. Commit with a HEREDOC message
5. Push to the current branch (`git push` or `git push -u origin HEAD` if needed)
6. Confirm the push succeeded in your reply (branch + short summary)

## Git safety (still required)

- Never update git config
- Never force-push to `main`/`master`
- Never skip hooks unless the user explicitly requests it
- Do not amend unless the user asked and the amend rules in user rules are satisfied

## Version bumps

For skin/addon changes in this project, bump `addon.xml` / `changelog.txt` versions when the change is user-visible, then include those files in the same commit.
